WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:04.560
- [Interviewer] Okay, all right so Asher

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.393
- Yes

00:00:05.393 --> 00:00:06.226
- [Interviewer] Asher
where did you grow up,

00:00:06.226 --> 00:00:07.059
where are you from?

00:00:07.059 --> 00:00:08.870
- I'm originally from Phoenix, Arizona.

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:10.766
My family is from the Midwest,

00:00:10.766 --> 00:00:14.140
but I lived with my dad
when I was very young,

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.700
my great-grandmother died
and we moved into her house

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.361
in northern Arizona and never left.

00:00:19.361 --> 00:00:21.360
- [Interviewer] And
how was your childhood?

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:26.210
- Abusive, but fun.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:28.070
I was a skateboarder so I had lots of fun.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.009
So the turmoil at my home
being from a broken family

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:36.960
and bouncing back and forth to
step-parents and weekend dad

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.330
and stuff like that sent me to
the street as a skateboarder

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:43.590
and that's what gave me
my identity as a young man

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:44.870
because everybody looks for something

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.670
to attach themselves to even
if you have a good home life,

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.770
and so for me, I found that in the street,

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:52.523
and I never turned back.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:56.733
- [Interviewer] And, so you
came to LA at what point?

00:00:57.826 --> 00:01:01.320
- I've actually am state raised

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.553
so I did my first prison term here in CYA

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:09.460
when I was about fourteen or fifteen

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:14.460
and I was arrested in Indio,
California crossing the border

00:01:14.609 --> 00:01:18.080
in a stolen vehicle that I was unaware of.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.900
My friends said hey, you
wanna go to Riverside,

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.500
and I said yeah sounds great,

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.210
and I fell asleep because
it was a long drive,

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:25.813
and on the way back they
said hey, we got pulled over

00:01:25.813 --> 00:01:29.110
tell the cops it's your car you know?

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.170
You're a juvenile, you won't go to jail.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.265
I learned really quickly
from that point on, you know,

00:01:33.265 --> 00:01:38.265
that the law and me have
had a long relationship

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:44.740
because I don't go with
the flow, you know?

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:46.630
So whatever someone tells me to do,

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:48.170
I typically tend to do the opposite.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.003
- [Interviewer] Where do you think you got

00:01:49.003 --> 00:01:50.540
that personality trait?

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:51.463
- My grandmother.

00:01:51.463 --> 00:01:52.296
(interviewer laughs)

00:01:52.296 --> 00:01:53.310
She was very stubborn.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:57.730
She was an artist, a
schoolteacher, she made pottery

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:00.160
and she was actually
the one that raised me

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.330
so eating vegetables, drinking water,

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:03.400
being a good hearted person,

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.080
all those traits come from my grandmother,

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:07.860
but the second that you go outside

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:10.370
you have to hide those
things and bury them

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.340
in order for self-preservation

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.780
and not necessarily put on
this facade of a tough guy

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:17.210
but you gotta put those things to a side

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.570
so I'll say I'm a split-personality

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:21.170
but I'm a chameleon in a sense

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:25.500
where I can change who I
am sometimes on an instant

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:30.500
but only for safety
reasons perhaps, you know?

00:02:30.707 --> 00:02:33.390
But my good nature comes
from my grandmother.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:35.590
- [Interviewer] So do you
have kids of your own?

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:39.604
- Yes, I have five children
and my oldest daughter

00:02:39.604 --> 00:02:42.610
is in her mid-twenties
and her name is Ashley.

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:44.996
I had her when I was very
young and at that time

00:02:44.996 --> 00:02:47.300
graffiti was something
that was a big deal to me

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.600
along with skateboarding.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:53.600
So I started writing my
daughter's name as Asher

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:59.030
as a way to show her how
much that I cared about her

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:03.440
and so, as she was growing
up she would see this

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:04.630
around the city and around town

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:06.530
and her friends when
she got older would say

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:10.290
oh look, there's your...look
look there's your name!

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:13.030
Your dad loves you so
much he writes your name!

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:15.253
And she's the polar opposite of me.

00:03:16.416 --> 00:03:21.416
When I say that, I mean
successful, smart, intelligent

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.670
and not a vandal and so
when you ask her her name

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.380
she says Ash.

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:33.330
When she signs her name
Ash-one but Asher is me

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.440
and Ashley is my daughter.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.675
All of my children not only like graffiti

00:03:39.675 --> 00:03:41.980
or either do it themselves

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:44.017
but they don't have a real love for it,

00:03:44.017 --> 00:03:46.770
it's just something that they enjoy

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:50.358
but I have five children and a grand child

00:03:50.358 --> 00:03:53.060
and I couldn't be happier.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.180
- [Interviewer] Did you raise them?

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:59.180
- Yes, except for my youngest
two, I have been incarcerated

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:04.550
but from birth until
my daughter was sixteen

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.070
she never went to day care,

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:08.980
she never went to grandma or grandpa's.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:12.540
I became a tattooer simply
for the fact to be able to

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.060
facilitate being a stay at home parent.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:20.060
So my first two kids are
very lucky to have had me

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.494
as such a big influence in their life

00:04:24.494 --> 00:04:25.830
and I think the reason why
they are such good, successful

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:30.830
people and not like me is
a big testament to that.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.410
- [Interviewer] So, what
do you call yourself?

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.360
A tagger, a graffiti artist?

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.376
- I'm one of Los Angeles,
California's most prolific

00:04:37.376 --> 00:04:40.470
graffiti writers because
not only do I dominate

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:44.040
the visual supremacy of downtown
LA with my block letters

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.470
and I paint in broad daylight

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:48.640
but I don't hide who I am
and I don't hide my face

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.341
because my grandmother told
me when I was very young

00:04:51.341 --> 00:04:55.280
if you have to sneak to
do something it's wrong

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:57.810
and so this is very confusing
to me because this now means

00:04:57.810 --> 00:05:01.160
that smoking marijuana,
cussing and spray painting

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:04.030
is something that society
might deem to be negative

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.800
but I don't wanna offend my grandmother.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.600
And so she's like well
I wouldn't do it then

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.370
if you're concerned about offending me.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.670
But this is who I am.

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:12.570
Well then you should be who you are.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:15.040
Well now I'm confused
so how do I be who I am

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.050
and not offend her?

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.108
So what she's trying to say is

00:05:18.108 --> 00:05:20.300
you just have to do what makes you happy.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:25.150
And so I decided that what
I'm doing is not a crime

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.530
if I don't believe it's a crime.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:29.140
So by changing the color of
the surface a millimeter thick

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.966
might be something that society deems

00:05:30.966 --> 00:05:34.430
not only a crime but a felonious crime

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.390
based upon how much property damage

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:39.130
and then can result in
not only incarceration

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:44.130
but community service,
restitution and even embarrassment

00:05:44.385 --> 00:05:47.150
being dragged to your court
and all kinds of things

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.288
simply because you're expressing yourself

00:05:49.288 --> 00:05:52.840
in a way that's not conducive
to what society deems

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:55.914
but this is very strange
because if you paint a mural

00:05:55.914 --> 00:05:57.850
then you will be not only celebrated,

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.870
but you will be financially compensated.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:01.960
So if I choose to go and put my art here,

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.848
that's not on somebody's personal property

00:06:03.848 --> 00:06:05.973
I can be arrested and I just think that

00:06:05.973 --> 00:06:08.540
that is ridiculous and fuckery
and I don't agree with it

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:10.800
because society has so many problems

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:14.870
but yet if I go up and
put my message, or my name

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:18.830
or whatever I want and
that's deemed illegal

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:21.430
but then there's a sign and then there's

00:06:22.707 --> 00:06:23.540
all these other things from the city,

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:25.120
and promotions for politicians

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:26.650
and everybody trying to get elected

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:30.514
and all of that is not only
illegal in it's own right

00:06:30.514 --> 00:06:32.470
but it's eye pollution

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:33.790
and it's something that
we don't wanna see.

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:35.788
Calvin Klein ads and things like that.

00:06:35.788 --> 00:06:38.856
Los Angeles, California's
diversity is based upon

00:06:38.856 --> 00:06:41.860
the fact that not only do
we celebrate graffiti here

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.950
but when you get well known enough

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:46.920
you're actually elevated
to celebrity status

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:50.290
which is kind of a conundrum
when you think about it.

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:53.010
If something is illegal and
then you're really good at it

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.310
then now you're an artist and
now you go to the art world

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:56.280
and make lots of money.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:58.710
But how do you bridge the
gap from being a tagger

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:01.220
and something illegal and
to make it into mainstream?

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:05.900
Well, I have found that
majority of people sell out,

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:07.260
I guess is what you would call it.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.690
They stop doing graffiti.

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:11.800
If they ever did do illegal
graffiti like myself,

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:13.070
they don't do it like I do.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:14.610
They sneak around at nighttime.

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:16.030
They wear hoods and masks.

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.190
They get drunk.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:18.270
They get liquid courage.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:19.410
They go into train yards.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.510
They get their friends around them

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:23.089
because they're scared to be
in these bad neighborhoods.

00:07:23.089 --> 00:07:26.210
Every day that I paint
in downtown Los Angeles

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:29.870
I am going to be confronted
by somebody in a negative way

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:30.703
and I know and understand this,

00:07:30.703 --> 00:07:33.070
and this is a risk that
I'm willing to take

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:35.480
but whether its an 18th street gang member

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.090
telling me that this is his territory

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:38.470
and that he's working here

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:42.160
or a security guard, a police
officer, a business owner,

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:44.610
another graffiti writer, anybody,

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:47.550
I'm going to run into
one of them guaranteed.

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:51.088
But what separates me, I don't fuckin run.

00:07:51.088 --> 00:07:52.810
Ever.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:53.960
I own that shit.

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:55.295
And so when somebody confronts you,

00:07:55.295 --> 00:07:58.676
not only do they not understand
why are you not running

00:07:58.676 --> 00:08:01.460
but they respect you for that,

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:02.930
even if it is their building

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:04.960
and you turn around and talk
to them and tell them why,

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:06.770
even if he doesn't agree with it,

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:08.810
he's not going to punch you, shoot you

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:10.560
because not only am I articulate

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:12.151
and I'm telling him exactly what I'm doing

00:08:12.151 --> 00:08:15.365
this is the first time that
he's ever spoken or confronted

00:08:15.365 --> 00:08:18.920
what he would consider a
tagger or a graffiti writer

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:23.550
and this guy is not what he thought.

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:27.450
And so my appearance and
my art looks abrasive

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:28.470
and I totally understand that,

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:29.750
because it's supposed to,

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:32.550
but it's a reflection of
who I am and where I'm from.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:35.461
So, doing what I do
here wouldn't make sense

00:08:35.461 --> 00:08:37.530
in another city or another place

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:39.090
because not only would
it not be celebrated,

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:40.330
it would be viewed as negative.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:43.663
But here people around the
world look at what I do here

00:08:43.663 --> 00:08:47.110
and copy it around the world.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:51.100
So to me that lets me know
not only do I have influence

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:55.090
but because I'm in Los Angeles, California

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:56.760
it makes it extremely different.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.523
Nobody cares if you paint in the middle of

00:08:59.523 --> 00:09:01.440
the wilderness in Colorado.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:04.021
Nobody gives a shit if
you go and do graffiti

00:09:04.021 --> 00:09:08.537
in the back of your
mom's backyard on a shed,

00:09:08.537 --> 00:09:10.500
no matter how impressive it is,

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:13.380
because there was no risk involved.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:16.830
So for me, that I think is
one of the biggest things

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:20.960
is that not only am I possibly
going to lose my freedom,

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:21.883
which I have.

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:25.878
Get beaten severely which
recently this was a result

00:09:25.878 --> 00:09:29.300
of some poor decisions on my behalf

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:32.655
directly caused from painting
and then the steps...

00:09:32.655 --> 00:09:34.950
- [Interviewer] Yeah you got
a couple black eyes right now.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:36.100
- Yes.

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:38.800
The black eyes, I was in a hospital

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.584
for a good day and a half.

00:09:40.584 --> 00:09:42.080
They had to do a lot of tests.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:45.430
I had some severe bleeding
issues not only in my face

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.270
but other areas of the body,

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:51.270
but I'm not sure how good
you can see these scars

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.580
but the one right here...

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:54.413
- [Interviewer] Oh yeah.

00:09:54.413 --> 00:09:58.320
- This was somebody's teeth.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:01.700
This one along the top was
my head being split open

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.103
with a pipe.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:07.310
This one across the forehead
I was beaten with hammers

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.340
in an alley not too far
from here because...

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:10.370
- [Interviewer] These are different?

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:12.387
- These are all different
instances but these are all

00:10:12.387 --> 00:10:17.387
injuries directly related to
graffiti because somebody,

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:22.370
in my opinion, did something
that they shouldn't have.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:26.640
Basically disrespected me, went over me,

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:27.930
wrote some stupid message

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:29.840
that was not conducive to reality.

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:32.410
They see me, they fall down really fast,

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:35.030
I leave very quickly and they tell on me.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:38.300
That's been a repetitive
cycle throughout my life

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:41.350
and at some point most graffiti writers,

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:44.500
at about from the age
of fourteen to twenty

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:47.450
they come faced with life decisions,

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:51.890
which is I got a job, I
got arrested, I have a kid,

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:54.966
this is juvenile activity
and I can't continue this.

00:10:54.966 --> 00:10:56.120
And so they stop.

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:59.350
Or here in Los Angeles,
this is something different

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:00.690
from a lot of places,

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:03.660
they write graffiti in the
neighborhood where they're from

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:07.550
but the gangs are so deep in these areas

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:09.630
where graffiti is predominant,

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.919
that the gangs confront
the people doing graffiti

00:11:11.919 --> 00:11:13.410
and now they tell them

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.260
hey, not only can you not do that here

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:17.310
but you're disrespecting us,
cause this is our territory

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:18.690
so by you writing your name

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:20.790
you're saying that this is your territory.

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:22.240
So instead of us fucking you up,

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.480
because we know who you
are and where you live,

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:27.090
we can just allow you
to keep doing graffiti

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:28.710
but now you're gonna write the gang name

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:30.370
because you're from this hood anyway.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:32.290
So the little kid who had no intention

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:34.306
of ever being a gang member

00:11:34.306 --> 00:11:37.660
because he was a little
writer, or tagger, or artist

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:39.370
is now a full fledged gang member

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:41.270
because he didn't have a choice.

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:43.930
He didn't want to, but now that he is,

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:47.250
he still gets to practice
that act of graffiti

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:51.300
and there's a lot of
gangs here in Los Angeles

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:54.543
that started as taggers
and their gang name

00:11:54.543 --> 00:11:57.949
is a tagger name but
now it's a full on gang.

00:11:57.949 --> 00:12:00.060
- [Interviewer] So you
been arrested for this?

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:03.210
- You know up until recently
I had never been arrested

00:12:04.463 --> 00:12:07.390
and prosecuted for graffiti.

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:10.450
I've been stopped, I get
stopped almost on a daily basis

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:11.460
and people don't understand this,

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.760
they want to know how
do you not get arrested?

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:15.700
Oh trust and believe
me, I do get arrested.

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:17.250
I've never been prosecuted.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:18.780
They've never filed charges.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:21.520
They've dismissed them, they've let me go,

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:23.970
I talked my way out of it, I you know,

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.140
things of that nature.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.226
But just recently I was arrested on

00:12:27.226 --> 00:12:30.330
East LA, Soto and Olympic,

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:32.530
underneath a bridge painting

00:12:33.490 --> 00:12:35.420
and I was with a group of people
that were from out of town

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:40.300
and they got, obviously,
a little agitated,

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:42.760
or not agitated but they
got a little concerned

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:43.593
when the police came.

00:12:43.593 --> 00:12:46.139
And I said don't worry about
it, I'll take care of it.

00:12:46.139 --> 00:12:47.700
And when I went and approached the police,

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.445
it's because I deal with
this on a daily basis

00:12:50.445 --> 00:12:54.090
and I thought that it wasn't
going to be a bad situation.

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:56.240
Unfortunately, I was wrong.

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:57.900
They told me to get down on the ground

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:01.270
and I was ultimately
arrested for felony vandalism

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:04.260
and when I went to court
the case was not filed

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:07.217
and I was very happy, but
I'm currently out on bail

00:13:07.217 --> 00:13:09.620
for an assault charge.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:12.462
And I got out of prison on my last case

00:13:12.462 --> 00:13:14.210
for aggravated assault,

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:17.070
which is the exact same charge
that I'm on bail for now.

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:19.790
But, when I got arrested for graffiti,

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:21.870
you cannot get arrested
while you're out on bail,

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:22.950
which I did.

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:24.350
So, I bailed out on that one

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:26.139
before my other bail
company could find out.

00:13:26.139 --> 00:13:29.500
But when I went to court, they dropped it.

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:31.690
Well I got a letter in the mail yesterday,

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:33.030
they just filed it.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:34.750
So not only did they just
file the graffiti charge

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.010
that I thought was dropped,

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:38.731
this incident with the black eyes,

00:13:38.731 --> 00:13:40.810
I got another assault case.

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:45.690
And so now, I'm on bail for assault case,

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:49.900
felony vandalism, got
an assault case pending,

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:51.840
all three of these pending,

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:55.700
and I still do graffiti every day.

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:57.920
- [Interviewer] So, let's
say I'm a business owner.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:58.753
- Okay.

00:13:58.753 --> 00:14:00.453
- [Interviewer] All right,
I rent a space somewhere.

00:14:01.688 --> 00:14:02.521
And I am proud of my new business...

00:14:02.521 --> 00:14:03.390
- Yes.

00:14:03.390 --> 00:14:05.407
And we clean it up and make it perfect

00:14:05.407 --> 00:14:06.260
and that's my new place of business.

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:08.070
And then one day I show up for work

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:10.388
and there's graffiti
all over the building.

00:14:10.388 --> 00:14:13.610
How do you justify that?

00:14:13.610 --> 00:14:14.443
- It depends on...

00:14:14.443 --> 00:14:15.780
- [Interviewer] Cause I didn't
approve it, I didn't want it.

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:19.140
- Absolutely, and so,
every graffiti writer

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:21.340
has certain things that
they're willing to respect.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:24.400
Me personally, I respect
people's personal property.

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:29.250
I would never write on
somebody's vehicle or their home.

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:31.180
Now, you mentioned a business,

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.390
it depends on where that
business is located.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:36.423
If you were in downtown LA
or in downtown Skid Row,

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:39.620
your shit's fair game and the reason being

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:41.630
is because it's such a bad neighborhood

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:45.340
that this artwork whether
it's gang writing,

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:49.930
traditional graffiti,
propaganda, wheat pasting,

00:14:49.930 --> 00:14:53.870
road signs, there's gonna
be some sort of graffiti

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.300
on your building whether I do
it or somebody else does it.

00:14:56.300 --> 00:15:00.220
But if you have a new
building in a nice area,

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:01.410
I would never touch that building.

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:04.610
And the reason being,
is because not only am I

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:06.980
a business man, and I have my own business

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:07.940
and my own studio,

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:09.820
I wouldn't want somebody
to do that to my shit.

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:13.090
But the thing of it is,
everybody's different.

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:16.553
So when I was painting on
a business very near here,

00:15:16.553 --> 00:15:18.570
the business owner came out

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:20.880
and in the commission of doing this

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:22.800
he threatened me with a gun

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:25.400
and said what in the
world would possess you

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:28.440
to stand here so brazenly and
disrespect me and my business?

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:32.463
And I said, I beg to
differ, what's your name?

00:15:32.463 --> 00:15:35.570
And he didn't want to shake my hand

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:38.040
but it caused him to pause,

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:39.660
and so when I asked him what his name was,

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:41.470
I said my name is Asher and
I'm actually your neighbor

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:42.303
and I live right down the street

00:15:42.303 --> 00:15:43.879
and I have a studio across the street

00:15:43.879 --> 00:15:45.864
and your building was covered with garbage

00:15:45.864 --> 00:15:47.570
and so I was covering it up in a way

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:48.830
that I thought looked better.

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:50.340
But I didn't mean to offend you

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.440
and you don't own this building,

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:53.800
but I understand that you own it

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:55.218
and now that I've met you,

00:15:55.218 --> 00:15:57.370
I won't continue to do this

00:15:57.370 --> 00:15:59.900
but since I started you should
at least allow me to finish.

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.358
And he said absolutely not,

00:16:01.358 --> 00:16:05.260
because I have this gun doesn't
mean I'm afraid to use it,

00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:06.880
but I don't like my neighbors whatsoever,

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:08.410
so please do it next door.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.880
So I just changed my camera
that I was recording,

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:13.400
and I shifted it and I went
and finished it next door.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:17.463
So, I mean, it kinda just
depends on a case by case basis.

00:16:18.434 --> 00:16:23.434
And I think in my view of things it's okay

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:30.290
but it's because it's already there

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:31.870
or it's already going to happen.

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:33.900
But I definitely wouldn't
want it on my home

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:37.240
or my business, a school, or a church.

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:39.660
You know, things of that
nature, but that's me.

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:42.250
I'm in my forties, I'm an old school guy,

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:46.590
but new kids, new people,
you have to give respect

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:47.800
in order to receive it

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:49.900
and if they're from the
street, if they're from a gang

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:51.490
and a crew that does this graffiti

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:53.280
and they're proud of being vandals

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.910
then that's what they wanna do.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:57.733
The point is to vandalize shit, you know?

00:16:57.733 --> 00:16:59.817
It's because they're seeking an identity

00:16:59.817 --> 00:17:03.110
and that's what it is
about is fuck the system,

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:05.114
stick it to the man, we don't pay taxes,

00:17:05.114 --> 00:17:09.890
we steal our supplies, we don't
abide by rules and a society

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:11.740
because it's a bunch of shit and lies

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:14.020
and we're artists, and
we're young, and we're free,

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:16.950
and we're fuckin wild and we
can do whatever we choose.

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:20.300
But, let's just be honest,
that self destructive behavior

00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:22.020
is only gonna get you so far.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:24.830
And so, I've been dealing
with this for a long time

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:27.280
and people ask me why
do you keep doing this?

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.680
Like, you have children,
you have grandchildren,

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:31.395
you're successful, you're celebrated,

00:17:31.395 --> 00:17:34.210
why haven't you started
doing something else?

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:37.633
Why haven't you sta...and
what do you get out of this?

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:39.663
Headaches.

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:41.363
Headaches.

00:17:41.363 --> 00:17:45.171
But it's my passion and it's
who I am and I don't believe

00:17:45.171 --> 00:17:49.110
that I'm gonna perish,
that I'm gonna go to jail.

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:51.610
Even though I'm a pendejo,
and I'm state raised

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:52.804
and this is who I am.

00:17:52.804 --> 00:17:54.980
I used to feel like this negativity

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:57.280
but now I realize that
this is not only who I am,

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:58.600
but it brought me to this point.

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:00.390
And so, if I didn't go
through those negativity

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:03.807
and those trials of prison,
especially as a young man,

00:18:03.807 --> 00:18:05.930
I wouldn't be where I am now.

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:10.930
But, unfortunately for me, I'm
still carrying a lot of that

00:18:11.254 --> 00:18:14.840
misperception of masculinity.

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:18.591
So, god forbid somebody step
on my shoes or bump into me

00:18:18.591 --> 00:18:20.820
because I'm gonna assault you immediately

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:21.940
without thinking about it.

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:24.970
And then, immediately after
doing so I'm gonna realize

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:27.268
oh shit, you messed up.

00:18:27.268 --> 00:18:31.169
And so, when I was young my
dad used to always ask me,

00:18:31.169 --> 00:18:33.070
even though we didn't live together,

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:34.070
he would always say

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:35.330
what's the matter with you?

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:36.163
What's the matter with you?

00:18:36.163 --> 00:18:37.010
You don't think!

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:38.650
What's the matter with you?

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:40.180
And it got to the point where
I started thinking there was

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:41.230
something wrong with me.

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:42.702
You know like, maybe I
do have a mental problem

00:18:42.702 --> 00:18:46.160
because if I punch this guy,

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:47.450
or if I paint on this guy's building

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:49.200
and I get arrested or I go to jail,

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:52.410
that's not only not smart,
but that's self destructive

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:53.800
so maybe he's right.

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:56.050
But in reality, it wasn't
until I started painting

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:58.720
severe consequences like going to jail,

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:03.720
like losing my freedom, like
being alienated from my family,

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:06.570
that I started to slowly
think about things.

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:08.773
But now fast forward
twenty five years later,

00:19:08.773 --> 00:19:10.533
why am I still doing it?

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:17.030
I don't believe I'm doing anything wrong.

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:19.060
I think society's the one with the problem

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:23.340
and I think that when I
have my first solo art show

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:26.180
in a gallery in downtown
Los Angeles this year,

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:28.180
and I make an extensive amount of money,

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:29.750
and then I start traveling the world,

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:30.680
now everybody's gonna say

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:33.990
oh look, this is my
nephew, this is my brother!

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:36.470
Oh look how proud I am
of my family member,

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:37.830
he's so successful!

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:39.870
And only because of monetary value

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:41.600
or because I'm doing it in a gallery?

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:43.519
So if I'm a successful tattooer

00:19:43.519 --> 00:19:45.003
instead of painting the street

00:19:45.003 --> 00:19:47.720
or instead of doing canvasses,

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:50.140
so I choose my canvass and I choose my art

00:19:50.140 --> 00:19:51.540
and where I choose to put it,

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:54.460
but you're only celebrated
in certain ways.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:56.695
And I think that that
is not only ridiculous

00:19:56.695 --> 00:19:59.920
but I am willing to deal
with the consequences

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:04.920
because, authenticity cannot
be faked or duplicated.

00:20:05.537 --> 00:20:09.750
And, real will always rise to the top.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:13.630
So, some people aren't the best hustlers,

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:16.480
some people can't sell their
art, some people have the best

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:19.788
art ability but don't have the hustle

00:20:19.788 --> 00:20:22.600
or the knowledge of finances.

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:26.179
My thing is, I have no fucking
interest in those things!

00:20:26.179 --> 00:20:29.757
I'm a minimalist and I love being out here

00:20:29.757 --> 00:20:32.440
and the fact that I'm
not doing life in prison,

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:35.280
the fact that I can walk outside my studio

00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:36.950
on Skid Row and for the price

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:38.181
of a dollar can of spray paint,

00:20:38.181 --> 00:20:40.260
paint anywhere in Los Angeles

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:42.728
knowing it'll reach to
the far ends of the world

00:20:42.728 --> 00:20:46.890
via the internet, I'm the
happiest guy on earth.

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:50.810
I might not have a dollar
to my name at some point.

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:54.210
I might be facing over a decade in prison.

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:55.890
Single.

00:20:55.890 --> 00:20:57.720
All these things against me.

00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:00.450
But in reality, I'm the
happiest that I've ever been

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:02.050
because I'm living my dream

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:04.088
and I don't care what anybody says,

00:21:04.088 --> 00:21:06.090
I'm a part of history.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:07.810
And not only am I in the history books,

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:10.360
I'm in the concrete in
downtown Los Angeles,

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:11.500
that shit is never going anywhere,

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:12.740
I'm in the history books.

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:14.200
I'm on the rooftop of this building,

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:16.047
the front of the street,
downtown, everywhere.

00:21:16.047 --> 00:21:21.047
OG Asher Lokes, downtown Skid
Row, Los Angeles, California.

00:21:21.488 --> 00:21:23.163
Watch out for me.

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:24.843
- [Interviewer] All right Asher.

00:21:24.843 --> 00:21:25.676
Thank you very much.

00:21:25.676 --> 00:21:27.380
- [Asher] Thank you.

